========================================================================
Part A -- card T3-LAT (N08-G2/G3): coordinate box vs log-convex hull
========================================================================
p = 2, n = 2, exponent coordinates v_j = val_2(x_j)

A1 box (2x2 square, E == B(E))
   box mins m = (0, 0)   =>  B(E) = { v : v1 >= 0, v2 >= 0 }
   E is itself a box: B(E) = E = conv(E)  ->  BOX
   mu(B(E)) = 1 ,  mu(conv E) = 1  (no gap)
  PASS  A-box-closes 

A2 diagonal {(0,0),(1,1)}
   box mins m = (0, 0)   =>  B(E) = { v : v1 >= 0, v2 >= 0 }
  PASS  x not in E (so B(E) strictly larger than E) 
  PASS  separator on E (phi.e = [0, 0], c = 0)
  PASS  separator at x (phi.x = -1 for x = (0, 1))
  PASS  => x in B(E) and x not in conv(E) -> NONBOX
   NONBOX: x = (0, 1) lies in the coordinate box but not in the log-convex hull
   mu(B(E)) = 1 ,  mu(conv E) = 0  (conv is lower-dimensional)
   => the log-convex hull is not even admissible here: the two
      hull conventions are not comparable as regions

A3 anti-diagonal {(0,1),(1,0)}
   box mins m = (0, 0)   =>  B(E) = { v : v1 >= 0, v2 >= 0 }
  PASS  x not in E (so B(E) strictly larger than E) 
  PASS  separator on E (phi.e = [1, 1], c = 1)
  PASS  separator at x (phi.x = 0 for x = (0, 0))
  PASS  => x in B(E) and x not in conv(E) -> NONBOX
   NONBOX: x = (0, 0) lies in the coordinate box but not in the log-convex hull
   mu(B(E)) = 1 ,  mu(conv E) = 0  (conv is lower-dimensional)
   => the log-convex hull is not even admissible here: the two
      hull conventions are not comparable as regions

Reading: `LocalTheory.hull` returns a hull REGION (b*O), i.e. exactly B(E).
So on a capsule whose exponent set is not a box the coordinate-box hull is
strictly larger than the log-convex hull; in the two NONBOX cases above the
latter has Haar measure 0 and is not an admissible region at all.  Hence
'hull = per-coordinate lambda*O' is a substantive claim about the container,
not a harmless relaxation -- the deviation is documented at Ind3.lean:32-38.
That is the precise form of N08-G2: it is a decidable property of E.

