Part B -- card T4-ATT (N07-H1): attainment vs strict certificate
========================================================================
M = log-vol(hull(VC(I))) = 1 ,   target t = qPilot.lhs = 3/4

M1 identified-copies shape: mu(out S) = mu(S)
   T1 yes, T2 yes, T3: mu <= M yes
   -> WITNESS : 3/4  (S of length 3/4)

M2 same fields, other out: mu(out S) = min(mu(S), M/2)
   T1 yes, T2 yes, T3: mu <= M yes
   -> CERTIFICATE : 1/2  (sup of the image is 1/2 < t = 3/4)

  PASS  M1 WITNESS 
  PASS  M1 witness inside hull 
  PASS  M2 CERTIFICATE 
  PASS  M2 certificate is strict 
  PASS  M2 (T3) still holds 
  PASS  fields do not decide 
Reading: the two models agree on every declared field of `EtaAlg D` that
Part B can see (T1 permutes S, T2 etUnitOnly, T3 'out(S) inside the hull'),
yet M1 attains the target and M2 does not.  Therefore the declared fields
alone give UNDETERMINED; a decision needs one more declared item (the
sup of the log-vol range of `out iota`).  This is exactly N07-H1: `out` is
a bare field and `realisation` (EtaAlg.lean:123) gives containment only.

